Add a VK_KHR_display Vulkan surface to the mali-fbdev video driver.

The backend owns a bare framebuffer -- no DRM, no GBM, no compositor -- so
SDL had no way to hand out a Vulkan surface and SDL_CreateWindow(SDL_WINDOW_
VULKAN) failed outright.  Emulators that ask SDL for their surface (PPSSPP)
could not use Vulkan on any fbdev board even with a working ICD installed;
RetroArch was unaffected only because it creates its own display surface.

VK_KHR_display is the whole answer here: the display is exclusive and its
mode is fixed, which is what a handheld running one fullscreen emulator
wants.  Modelled on SDL_kmsdrmvulkan.c, minus the DRM half, and with three
changes it needs on vendor blobs: fall back to physical device 0 when none
reports as a GPU, never try vkCreateDisplayModeKHR (the panel mode is fixed
and the blobs reject it), and test plane alpha as a bitmask rather than for
equality.

configure.ac already globs src/video/mali-fbdev/*.c, so the new file needs
no build wiring.

